314
02:12:44.000 --> 02:13:18.000
How do you make that stuff happen and dream big? Yeah, I mean, we're also in such a different political landscape in terms of power now than we were back then too. Now private interests, special interests have much more sophisticated lobbies. The power of the state was much stronger back then. There was no CBO score and budget hawks back then.
你是如何把那些事情变成现实并胸怀大志的？对，我的意思是，就权力而言，我们现在所处的政治环境也与当年大不相同了。现在私人利益和特殊利益集团拥有更加成熟的游说力量。当年的国家权力要强大得多。那时候没有什么国会预算办公室（CBO）评分和预算鹰派。

315
02:13:18.000 --> 02:13:55.000
But I think now, what it requires too is, is different techniques and a willingness to experiment. I think a lot of times folks talk about efficacy and they'll say like, you hear this all the time. I hate this phrase in DC. They go, oh, I'm not a show horse. I'm a work horse. And it's like, so you're just giving up the entire mantle of public power and the interest of public power?
但我认为现在，它还需要的是不同的技巧以及尝试的意愿。我觉得很多时候人们谈论效能时，他们会说，你总是能听到这种说法。我讨厌华盛顿特区的这种说辞。他们会说，哦，我不是表演型政客，我是实干家。这就好像是说，你放弃了公共权力的整个使命以及公共权力的利益？

316
02:13:55.000 --> 02:14:34.000
It is a part of being effective. And we can't moralize or consider some avenues as more or less virtuous than others. I think that for me, when it comes to implementation, we rallied enormous public interest and continue to rally enormous public interest. And I think like in DC, that's considered dirty or like low brow. And I just lean into it because I'm like, great, Elaine unto myself. I have no competition.
这是发挥效能的一部分。我们不能进行道德说教，也不能认为某些途径比其他途径更有或更没有美德。我认为对我来说，在执行方面，我们调动了巨大的公众利益，并且继续在调动巨大的公众利益。我觉得在华盛顿特区，这被认为是肮脏的或低俗的。而我只是顺应它，因为我想，太好了，这正合我意。我没有任何竞争对手。

317
02:14:34.000 --> 02:15:05.000
Like, I'm from the Bronx, I don't care. I don't care about like if it's high brow or low brow, like it's there, I'm gonna use it. But then on top of that, okay, then you hit the institutional power. This will never get passed, you know. I pissed off all of the gatekeepers and ring holders and all that, and it gets to a point where then they just don't want to move anything out of spite, right? Like you didn't kiss the ring, you didn't do the proper things,
就像我来自布朗克斯区一样，我不在乎。我不在乎这是阳春白雪还是下里巴人，既然它摆在那儿，我就要利用它。但不仅如此，好吧，接着你就会撞上体制权力。你知道的，这永远通不过。我惹恼了所有的守门人、权柄掌握者以及诸如此类的人，事情发展到一定程度，他们就会仅仅出于怨恨而不想推动任何进展，对吧？就像你没有向权势低头，你没有做那些规矩的事情，

318
02:15:05.000 --> 02:15:42.000
so like we're not gonna move it. And that was, I think, the story of those early days. And so then I kind of look around and I say, okay, what other levers can I use? I don't need to pass this thing, to do the thing, actually, because it's passed in the public consciousness. And so what I started to do was to look for these small ways and unnoticed ways. And so I started to turn to how do I do things without my name being on it and without Green New Deal being on it, but it actually being a Green New Deal project.
所以我们就不打算推进它。我认为这就是早期那些日子的写照。因此，我环顾四周然后心想，好吧，我还能利用哪些其他杠杆？实际上，我不需要通过这个法案来办成这件事，因为它已经在公众意识中通过了。所以我开始做的是，寻找这些微小的、不引人注意的途径。于是我开始转向，如何在不把我的名字挂在上面、不把“绿色新政”挂在上面的情况下做事情，但它实际上就是一个“绿色新政”项目。

